/-
# 2-groups with the minimum condition on abelian subgroups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 3.56)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.56 (S. P. Strunkov): is a `2`-group with
the minimum condition for abelian subgroups locally finite?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupMinAbelianLocallyFiniteKourovka3Problem56Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.56 (S. P.
Strunkov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700204 (`KOU-3.56`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A `2`-group is a group in which every element has `2`-power order (Mathlib's `IsPGroup 2`), not
necessarily finite. The minimum condition for abelian subgroups is well-foundedness of the abelian
subgroups under inclusion (every non-empty set of abelian subgroups has a minimal member). Locally
finite (the subgroup generated by every finite set is finite) is `IsLocallyFinite` of the Kourovka
1.23 entry, reused here. For large primes `p` the analogous statement fails (Olshanskii's Tarski
monsters: infinite `p`-groups all of whose proper non-trivial subgroups have order `p`).
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

/-- `G` satisfies the minimum condition on abelian subgroups: the abelian subgroups, ordered by
inclusion, are well founded (every nonempty set of them has a minimal element, equivalently there
is no infinite strictly descending chain of abelian subgroups). -/
def MinConditionAbelianSubgroups (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  WellFoundedLT {H : Subgroup G // ∀ a ∈ H, ∀ b ∈ H, a * b = b * a}

/-- Kourovka 3.56 (S. P. Strunkov): every `2`-group (every element has `2`-power order) with the
minimum condition on abelian subgroups is locally finite. -/
def twoGroupMinAbelianLocallyFinite : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsPGroup 2 G → MinConditionAbelianSubgroups G → IsLocallyFinite G

/--
Resolved true: Shunkov proves that a `2`-group satisfying the minimum condition for abelian
subgroups is locally finite; the Kourovka Archive answers 3.56 "Yes, it is". Source: E. I. Khukhro
and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.56 (S. P. Strunkov); resolution: V.
P. Shunkov, On a class of p-groups, Algebra and Logic 9 (1970), 291-297, Kourovka Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 3.56: Yes, it is, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02219449.
-/
public theorem_wanted twoGroupMinAbelianLocallyFinite_holds : twoGroupMinAbelianLocallyFinite

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupMinAbelianLocallyFiniteKourovka3Problem56Wanted
